## Limitations

* HTTP/1.1 over plain sockets; no HTTP/2, no proxy support (inject your own `Fetcher` if needed).
* Health is status-based: a 200 response with an error page is `healthy`.
* The system resolver cannot be interrupted; a lookup that exceeds the budget is abandoned in a
  daemon thread. `check_many` is sequential (the checker holds no state, so it may be shared
  between threads).
* NAT64, 6to4 and Teredo addresses are refused as a whole.
* Any TCP port of a public address may be checked: there is no port allow-list.
* Only `linkcheck/fetcher.py` imports `socket`: a policy that restricts network libraries per
  module must allow-list that file.

## Rollback

Delete `linkcheck/`, `tests/linkcheck/` and this page and revert the CHANGELOG entry. Nothing else
imports the package and no data is created or migrated.
